# Production entry point for https://3d-avatar.novaeuropa.space behind a Cloudflare Tunnel.
#
#   browser --HTTPS--> Cloudflare --tunnel, opened outbound from this machine--> cloudflared
#           --> Caddy http://127.0.0.1:8081 (this file) --> static site + /tts proxy
#
# Cloudflare terminates HTTPS, so Caddy serves plain HTTP on loopback only: no public port is
# open and no port forwarding is needed. For direct hosting with Caddy's own certificates
# (ports 80/443 forwarded to this machine), run Caddy with Caddyfile.direct instead.
# Environment (set by the systemd unit): SITE_ROOT, LOG_DIR.
{
	servers {
		# Requests arrive from cloudflared on loopback; take the visitor's address from
		# Cloudflare's header so logs show real clients.
		trusted_proxies static 127.0.0.1/32 ::1/128
		client_ip_headers Cf-Connecting-Ip X-Forwarded-For
	}
}

http://:8081 {
	bind 127.0.0.1
	import site.caddy
}
